 "result": "The package is `tessel`, not Flask, and all of this is in `src/tessel/views.py`.\n\n**Making the view function**\n- `View.to_view_func` (line 86) is a classmethod that builds the view function.\n- Inside it, a closure `view(**kwargs)` (lines 106 and 115) creates `self = cls(...)` and returns `active_app.ensure_sync(self.run_view)(**kwargs)`.\n  - If `init_every_request` is True, the default, a new instance is made on every request.\n  - If it is False, one instance is shared across requests.\n- It copies metadata onto the function, including `view.methods = cls.methods` (line 133). The router uses that attribute for the allowed HTTP methods.\n\n**Routing each HTTP method**\n- `VerbView(View)` (line 138) is the class that dispatches to `get()` and `post()`.\n- `VerbView.__init_subclass__` (line 165) builds `cls.methods` automatically. It adds the uppercased name of each HTTP-verb method the class defines (`get` becomes `GET`), and it merges in the `methods` of base classes. It skips this if the class sets `methods` itself.\n- `VerbView.run_view` (line 182) does the dispatch. It calls `getattr(self, request.method.lower(), None)` and runs the result through `active_app.ensure_sync(meth)(**kwargs)`. Line 188 falls back to `get` when the method is `HEAD` and there is no `head` handler.\n\n`View.run_view` (line 78) is the hook that `VerbView` overrides.",
